{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791231552,"nonce":"yYHKI2z8hVjuxVjf1alWI59/9zI=","title":"UI shader leftovers: even-odd clip fill, notch side colours, notch hit-testing","message":"What the UI shader port (f825df1) left, each small:\n- **Even-odd fill for clip paths.** clip-path polygons and paths fill by the non-zero rule only. CSS's `clip-path: polygon(evenodd, ...)` and `path(evenodd, ...)` need the even-odd rule. Blinc has no API for it to follow (blinc_gpu/src/path.rs only has a debug switch, BLINC_FILL_RULE_EVENODD), so ashui can add it itself: a fill-rule flag on the clip record and a crossing-count test in the clip shader.\n- **Per-side border colours on notched corners.** A box with a notch draws its whole border in the top side's colour.\n- **Hit-testing by a notch's outline.** Pointer hits use the box's rounded rectangle, so a press in a notch's cut-out still lands on the element.","files":null}]}